 },
 "_doc": "Bitou 'TAX INVOICE / BELASTINGFAKTUUR' (same 'Balance brought forward ... ** Total monthly' family as Breede Valley / Blue Crane, own rules). Header: ACCOUNT NUMBER after the town code, DATE OF ACCOUNT, Tax Invoice, the municipality's 'VAT No. / BTW Nommer', SITE; account summary 'TOTAL VAT | DUE DATE | ARREARS | CURRENT | AMOUNT DUE'; meter table W / E (kWh: prev, new, consumption, dd/mm-dd/mm) / K (demand kVA). THE PDF TEXT OVERPRINTS NEIGHBOURING CHARGE LINES: two lines often land on one text line with their digits fused ('aaaa.aabbbb.bb   cccc.ccdddd.dd' = VAT a + b, AMOUNT c + d). Every rule therefore reads both the clean 'VAT  AMOUNT' pair and the fused 'VAT1VAT2  AMT1AMT2' form (money always has exactly 2 decimals, so the split is unambiguous); fused kWh/kVA unit counts are NOT split - kWh comes from the E meter row, demand kVA from the K row, NMD kVA only when its line is clean. AMOUNT is VAT-inclusive. Electricity lines: Cons@ (energy -> standard_r, ex = AMOUNT - VAT), 'KVA Demand KVALS' x3 in fixed order: basic (units 1 -> other_r), demand (-> demand_r), NMD (-> nmd_r); on KVALS lines the 5-decimal column is the ex-VAT amount. total_ex_vat_r = sum(AMOUNT) - sum(VAT) over all electricity pairs; basic and NMD read from their 5-decimal amounts, demand_r = total - energy - basic - NMD (it equals the printed 5-decimal demand amount on 10/10, so the split is verified, but CHARGE=SUM is by construction). IDENTITY bit_vat_ex_r = electricity AMOUNT - (printed TOTAL VAT - the VAT of the Water:BUSS lines): exact on 10/10. 10/10 routed, 0 checks. Fingerprint: municipality VAT number + BITOU."
}